# Binary fixtures — committed bytes, not text. Marking them stops
# `git diff` from trying to wrap-print the binary and `git merge`
# from attempting a 3-way text merge that would corrupt the file.
# (Recorded adapter fixtures should be added here as they land.)

# Go sources, module files and shell scripts are LF everywhere: a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true otherwise fails gofmt and
# `go mod tidy -diff` in `make check`.
*.go text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Recorded MaxTime fixtures: byte-for-byte as recorded, never converted.
internal/vendors/maxtime/testdata/*.json -text
